## Test Strategy Template

When creating a test strategy document, use this structure:

```markdown
# [Feature Name] Test Strategy

## Test Scope
- Feature description
- Components to test
- Dependencies

## Test Categories

### 1. Positive Tests (Target: 40 tests)
**Scenarios**:
- [ ] List of positive test scenarios

**Test IDs**: TC-[FEATURE]-POS-001 through TC-[FEATURE]-POS-040

### 2. Negative Tests (Target: 20 tests)
**Scenarios**:
- [ ] Invalid inputs
- [ ] Missing required fields
- [ ] Authorization failures
- [ ] Non-existent resources

**Test IDs**: TC-[FEATURE]-NEG-001 through TC-[FEATURE]-NEG-020

### 3. Edge Cases (Target: 15 tests)
**Scenarios**:
- [ ] Boundary values
- [ ] Extreme inputs
- [ ] Timing edge cases
- [ ] Special characters

**Test IDs**: TC-[FEATURE]-EDGE-001 through TC-[FEATURE]-EDGE-015

### 4. Validation & Security (Target: 15 tests)
**Scenarios**:
- [ ] SQL injection prevention
- [ ] XSS prevention
- [ ] IDOR prevention
- [ ] Required field validation
- [ ] OWASP coverage

**Test IDs**: TC-[FEATURE]-SEC-001 through TC-[FEATURE]-SEC-015

### 5. Concurrency (Target: 10 tests)
**Scenarios**:
- [ ] Concurrent updates
- [ ] Race conditions
- [ ] Double submit
- [ ] Deadlock prevention

**Test IDs**: TC-[FEATURE]-CONC-001 through TC-[FEATURE]-CONC-010

## Total Tests: 100
## Estimated Effort: [X] hours
## Priority: Critical/High/Medium
```

