## Pre-Implementation Checklist

Before starting test implementation, verify:

- [ ] **All 5 categories included** in test strategy
- [ ] **Test count targets** defined for each category
- [ ] **OWASP Top 10 coverage** planned (if applicable)
- [ ] **Negative scenarios** cover all error paths
- [ ] **Edge cases** include boundary values and extreme inputs
- [ ] **Security tests** address injection and authorization
- [ ] **Concurrency tests** cover race conditions
- [ ] **Test IDs** follow consistent naming convention
- [ ] **Priority** assigned to each category
- [ ] **Dependencies** identified (test data, services, etc.)

---

## Post-Implementation Verification

After completing test implementation, verify:

- [ ] **All 5 categories implemented** with actual tests
- [ ] **Positive tests** cover all happy path scenarios
- [ ] **Negative tests** verify all error handlers work
- [ ] **Edge cases** confirm graceful degradation
- [ ] **Security tests** pass (no vulnerabilities found)
- [ ] **Concurrency tests** pass (no data corruption)
- [ ] **Documentation complete** with JSDoc comments
- [ ] **Test execution** successful in dev environment
- [ ] **Code coverage** meets minimum threshold (80%+)
- [ ] **Performance benchmarks** within acceptable range

